    "globalConstraints": "- The `pinned` cell has no schema `default`, on `todos` or on `trash`: a todo that is not pinned has no `pinned` cell at all, so every seed and expected file checked in before the cell existed loads to itself byte for byte. A `default` on any cell or value this plan adds is a finding.\n- Nothing under `state-exams/posted/` is written by a person or by a task: the driver writes `state-exams/posted/<producer task id>.json` from the producer's `state.reached` post before the consumer's exam first runs, and `.gitignore` keeps the directory out of every patch, so no posted file reaches the integration branch or the pull request. A task that creates, edits or checks in a file under `state-exams/posted/` is a finding.\n- Task 2's exam reads its seed from `state-exams/posted/1.json` and from nothing under `state-exams/seeds/`; an exam that falls back to a seed file when the posted file is absent is a finding \u2014 an absent post is the handshake's `absent` case and must stay visible.\n- The Pin button follows the Delete button inside every `.todoItem`: the exams already on the tree click a row's Delete as the first `.todoItem button`, and a button placed before it would take that click.\n- The linter's four test files under `packages/tinyapp-lint/test/` keep their count and list pins loosened only to containment and tree-computed counts, never re-pinned to a new exact literal (both folds of 2026-09-15).",
